rf.menu.sleepscreen.tips1=Good night, 
rf.menu.sleepscreen.tips2=! Here's a tip:

rf.menu.deathquote.1=IT APPEARS YOU HAVE REACHED AN END.
rf.menu.deathquote.2=WILL YOU TRY AGAIN?
rf.menu.deathquote.3=WILL YOU PERSIST?
rf.menu.deathquote.4=VERY INTERESTING.
rf.menu.deathquote.5=YOUR LOSS HERE IS ALL BUT GUARANTEED.
rf.menu.deathquote.6=AND YET YOU PERSIST...
rf.menu.deathquote.7=IF YOU ARE SO DETERMINED TO TRY ONCE MORE...
rf.menu.deathquote.8=THEN... SHALL WE HASTEN?
rf.menu.deathquote.9=AND SO, YOU MEET WITH THE SAME FATE.
rf.menu.deathquote.10=SHALL YOU TRY ONCE MORE?
rf.menu.deathquote.11=YOU ARE MISSING SOMETHING IMPORTANT.
rf.menu.deathquote.12=YOU WON'T WIN LIKE THIS.
rf.menu.deathquote.13=STILL... WILL YOU PERSIST?
rf.menu.deathquote.14=A LITTLE FURTHER.
rf.menu.deathquote.15=BUT IT... IS STILL WAITING.
rf.menu.deathquote.16=HOW MUCH LONGER NOW?
rf.menu.deathquote.17=YOU FAILED TO ACHIEVE ANY MARKS.
rf.menu.deathquote.18=WHAT ARE YOU?
rf.menu.deathquote.19=I VERY MUCH LOOK FORWARD TO THE NEXT.
rf.menu.deathquote.20=I imagine death so much, it feels more like a memory!
rf.menu.deathquote.21=You cannot give up just yet... 
rf.menu.deathquote.22=Stay determined...
rf.menu.deathquote.23=Sayonara!
rf.menu.deathquote.24=Come on, you can do better than that!
rf.menu.deathquote.25=Try harder... more harder!
rf.menu.deathquote.26=Skill issue!
rf.menu.deathquote.27=Well, it seems that your journey has ended. 
rf.menu.deathquote.28=Very sorry about that.
rf.menu.deathquote.29=Respawn yourself, NOW!
rf.menu.deathquote.30=gg no re
rf.menu.deathquote.31=You're a deathkisser!
rf.menu.deathquote.32=let's just get to the point.
rf.menu.deathquote.33=Next time, be prepared!
rf.menu.deathquote.34=Does death hurt?
rf.menu.deathquote.35=That one really knocked your socks off!
rf.menu.deathquote.36=So long, gay Bowser!
rf.menu.deathquote.37=SURPRISE!
rf.menu.deathquote.38=WASTED
rf.menu.deathquote.39=Perhaps I treated you too harshly.
rf.menu.deathquote.40=Do better next time... if there is one.
rf.menu.deathquote.41=Get off Minecraft for the day, you need it.
rf.menu.deathquote.42=It looks like you got your head handed to you. 
rf.menu.deathquote.43=So, how about giving it another shot?
rf.menu.deathquote.44=Thank you for choosing... exotic butters
rf.menu.deathquote.45=TOO BAD.
rf.menu.deathquote.46=Oh no! ... anyway
rf.menu.deathquote.47=Oops, you have to put the CD in your computer!
rf.menu.deathquote.48=PRESS 'R' TO TRY AGAIN
rf.menu.deathquote.49=In this world, it's kill or be killed!
rf.menu.deathquote.50=YOU ARE DEAD. NOT BIG SURPRISE.
rf.menu.deathquote.51=It's joever
rf.menu.deathquote.52=YOU'RE FINISHED!
rf.menu.deathquote.53=... and that's all she wrote!
rf.menu.deathquote.54=That's all, folks!
rf.menu.deathquote.55=Mamma mia, a-here I go again!
rf.menu.deathquote.56=Snake? Snake!? SNAAAAAKE!!
rf.menu.deathquote.57=The end is never the end!
rf.menu.deathquote.58=MAMAAAAAAAAA, I DON'T WANNA DIE
rf.menu.deathquote.59=FISSION MAILED
rf.menu.deathquote.60=One more time?
rf.menu.deathquote.61=You're right, terrible - let's try that again!
rf.menu.deathquote.62=Maybe try peaceful mode?
rf.menu.deathquote.63=This is NOT epic!
rf.menu.deathquote.64=This is not your fate...!
rf.menu.deathquote.65=Please, don't give up!
rf.menu.deathquote.66=Come on, that all you got!?
rf.menu.deathquote.67=You beefed it!
rf.menu.deathquote.68=Better luck next time, boss!
rf.menu.deathquote.69=Breathe in... breathe out...
rf.menu.deathquote.70=Check your pulse!
rf.menu.deathquote.71=You blacked out!
rf.menu.deathquote.72=GOD DAMN IT
rf.menu.deathquote.73=We all fail, we all make mistakes, it's what makes us human.
rf.menu.deathquote.74=Oof!
rf.menu.deathquote.75=geeettttttt dunked on!!!
rf.menu.deathquote.76=if we're really friends... you won't come back.
rf.menu.deathquote.77=Just be glad you're not on Bedrock Edition.
rf.menu.deathquote.78=Hope you weren't playing on Hardcore Mode!
rf.menu.deathquote.79=This is all just a bad dream... and you're NEVER waking up!
rf.menu.deathquote.80=Close your eyes, you'll be here soon
rf.menu.deathquote.81=[Die Now] AND I'LL THROW IN [50] [Bullets] FOR FREE!
rf.menu.deathquote.82=I'M SO [Proud] OF YOU, I COULD [Killed] YOU!
rf.menu.deathquote.83=[InsertPlayerName]'S [Hyperlink] WAS [Blocked]!!
rf.menu.deathquote.84=I'LL CHASE YOU TO THE ENDS OF THE EARTH!
rf.menu.deathquote.85=You never cease to surprise me.
rf.menu.deathquote.86=Well, what can I say? I die hard!
rf.menu.deathquote.87=[EXTREMELY LOUD INCORRECT BUZZER]
rf.menu.deathquote.88=This is your final frontier!
rf.menu.deathquote.89=Womp womp!
rf.menu.deathquote.90=Don't worry, your stuff won't despawn!
rf.menu.deathquote.91=No, the journey doesn't end here.
rf.menu.deathquote.92=I am... inevitable.
rf.menu.deathquote.93=Reincarnation in progress...
rf.menu.deathquote.94=Death is just another path, one that we all must take.
rf.menu.deathquote.95=It's past your bedtime!
rf.menu.deathquote.96=You've made a grave mistake!
rf.menu.deathquote.97=lol
rf.menu.deathquote.98=lmao, even
rf.menu.deathquote.99=There is no escape.
rf.menu.deathquote.100=There is an image of death in every birth.
rf.menu.deathquote.101=But still just OK...
rf.menu.deathquote.102=I don't feel so good...
rf.menu.deathquote.103=git gud
rf.menu.deathquote.104=The Past still haunts you.
rf.menu.deathquote.105=[LIFE SUPPORT: OFFLINE]
rf.menu.deathquote.106=Body desecrated. You lost 0 Cells.
rf.menu.deathquote.107=What, were you playing with a steering wheel?
rf.menu.deathquote.108=Say pal, you don't look so good.
rf.menu.deathquote.109=HIGHWAY TO HELL!
rf.menu.deathquote.110=This is how you died.
rf.menu.deathquote.111=sentenced to forever broccoli no candy
rf.menu.deathquote.112=hrngh soup
rf.menu.deathquote.113=But it refused.
rf.menu.deathquote.114=The Phantoms have put you in a deep sleep.
rf.menu.deathquote.115=Not with a bang, but a whimper.
rf.menu.deathquote.116=Roll it again.
rf.menu.deathquote.117=How abnormal...
rf.menu.deathquote.118=... and so he vanished, another number among the missing.
rf.menu.deathquote.119=But when the world needed him most, he vanished.
rf.menu.deathquote.120=Don't try this at home!
rf.menu.deathquote.121=Now it's time for another vendetta!
rf.menu.deathquote.122=I always come back!
rf.menu.deathquote.123=I DON'T WANT TO DIE.
rf.menu.deathquote.124=Fear is the mind-killer.
rf.menu.deathquote.125=VILLAGERS ARE DEAD THE NETHER IS FULL LAVA IS FUEL
rf.menu.deathquote.126=All those moments will be lost in time, like tears in rain.
rf.menu.deathquote.127=It's over, isn't it?
rf.menu.deathquote.128=In the Exodus, no one can hear you scream.
rf.menu.deathquote.129=The Exodus consumes all.
rf.menu.deathquote.130=28 STAB WOUNDS!
rf.menu.deathquote.131=New life will be born beneath the blood-stained sand!
rf.menu.deathquote.132=Did you have lead in your hotbar again?
rf.menu.deathquote.133=... and you get to tend the rabbits.
rf.menu.deathquote.134=This truly was a Raspberry Flavoured!
rf.menu.deathquote.135=Okay campers, rise and shine!
rf.menu.deathquote.136=The only true death is to never live.
rf.menu.deathquote.137=That's rough, buddy.
rf.menu.deathquote.138=Gamers don't die, they respawn!
rf.menu.deathquote.139=You missed that one, try another!
rf.menu.deathquote.140=Insert MineCoin to Continue
rf.menu.deathquote.141=[Give Up]   [Call Luigi]
rf.menu.deathquote.142=He was so ugly that everyone died. The End.
rf.menu.deathquote.143=One day you will mine your last block
rf.menu.deathquote.144=You must DIE!
rf.menu.deathquote.145=Ruh roh!
rf.menu.deathquote.146=They dug too greedily and too deep.
rf.menu.deathquote.147=The game was over and the player woke up from the dream.
rf.menu.deathquote.148=He was destroyed!
rf.menu.deathquote.149=The broom closet ending was my favorite!
rf.menu.deathquote.150=Maybe Go Fish is more our speed...
rf.menu.deathquote.151=We folded like a cheap suit!
rf.menu.deathquote.152=Time for us to shuffle off and try again!
rf.menu.deathquote.153=You know what they say, the house always wins!
rf.menu.deathquote.154=Looks like we found out who the real Joker is!
rf.menu.deathquote.155=Oh no, were you bluffing too?
rf.menu.deathquote.156=Looks like the joke's on us!
rf.menu.deathquote.157=If I had hands I would have covered my eyes!
rf.menu.deathquote.158=I'm literally a fool, what's your excuse?
rf.menu.deathquote.159=What a flop!
rf.menu.deathquote.160=Shoot like a star or fold like a quitter!
rf.menu.deathquote.161=Are you feeling alive?
rf.menu.deathquote.162=Are you feeling down?
rf.menu.deathquote.163=Have you lost control?
rf.menu.deathquote.164=Is your life a mess?
rf.menu.deathquote.165=Do your friends despise you?
rf.menu.deathquote.166=When did you start being yourself?
rf.menu.deathquote.167=...
rf.menu.deathquote.168=THERE IS NO ESCAPE
rf.menu.deathquote.169=IS THERE NO ESCAPE?
rf.menu.deathquote.170=TAKEN BY THE STYX
rf.menu.deathquote.171=TIME CANNOT BE STOPPED
rf.menu.deathquote.172=CAN TIME NOT BE STOPPED?
rf.menu.deathquote.173=Return to shadow, now!
rf.menu.deathquote.174=Special delivery: PAIN!
rf.menu.deathquote.175=No, my only weakness - dying!
rf.menu.deathquote.176=We ain't!

rf.menu.tip.1=Found an issue? Talk about it in the RF Discord!
rf.menu.tip.2=Got a suggestion? Talk about it in the RF Discord!
rf.menu.tip.3=Wanna chat with other RF players? Join the RF Discord!
rf.menu.tip.4=Sleeping won't skip nights instantly.
rf.menu.tip.5=Sleeping speeds up various processes.
rf.menu.tip.6=Zombies drop Cloth Scraps, used for making Beds... but you know that already.
rf.menu.tip.7=Having an Atlas in your hotbar will display a minimap.
rf.menu.tip.8=Bellows make fires last longer and speed up Furnaces, Ovens and Forges.
rf.menu.tip.9=Bombs damage mobs, but not blocks.
rf.menu.tip.10=Campfires grant Comfort when lit and stood near.
rf.menu.tip.11=Crushing Cinnabar yields Redstone Dust.
rf.menu.tip.12=Cooking Pots make meals and drinks that grant helpful effects.
rf.menu.tip.13=Ovens cook meals and pastries that grant helpful effects.
rf.menu.tip.14=Blaze Burners with Cooking Guides can cook automatically.
rf.menu.tip.15=There are no Stone tools - only Copper tools.
rf.menu.tip.16=Chainmail armor, Horse armor, Saddles and Name Tags are craftable in RF.
rf.menu.tip.17=Creeper Spores spawn a horde of friendly Creepies when thrown.
rf.menu.tip.18=Creepers won't damage terrain, but they will spawn Creepies.
rf.menu.tip.19=The crosshair indicates your tool's effectiveness on the block in front of you.
rf.menu.tip.20=Use a Pickaxe on Crying Obsidian to extract a Lachryte Tear.
rf.menu.tip.21=Lachryte Tears can be melted down into Liquefied Lachryte.
rf.menu.tip.22=Liquefied Lachryte is required to create a Nether Portal.
rf.menu.tip.23=Upon death, a totem will appear at your death point which holds your items.
rf.menu.tip.24=Discs can be smashed into fragments, which can be crafted into other discs.
rf.menu.tip.25=A Diving Helmet and Backtanks will let you traverse underwater more easily.
rf.menu.tip.26=Dunes are lush, two-toned deserts with Yucca trees and various other flora.
rf.menu.tip.27=Leather armor protects against fall damage.
rf.menu.tip.28=Chainmail armor damages attackers.
rf.menu.tip.29=Copper armor has a unique effect when struck by lightning.
rf.menu.tip.30=Golden tools increase drops from certain blocks and mobs.
rf.menu.tip.31=Golden armor lightly protects against fire.
rf.menu.tip.32=Iron armor provides light knockback resistance.
rf.menu.tip.33=Rose Gold tools dig quickly and cause blocks to drop in their purest form.
rf.menu.tip.34=Rose Gold armor protects against magic.
rf.menu.tip.35=Steel tools dig slowly, but are durable and knock targets further away.
rf.menu.tip.36=Steel armor provides good knockback resistance.
rf.menu.tip.37=Diamond equipment is obtained by upgrading Iron equipment with Diamond Plating.
rf.menu.tip.38=Diamond armor protects against projectile damage.
rf.menu.tip.39=Electrum tools dig very quickly and deal extra damage when sprinting.
rf.menu.tip.40=Electrum armor grants a movement speed boost.
rf.menu.tip.41=Netherite tools light targets on fire and smelt mined blocks.
rf.menu.tip.42=Netherite armor protects against fire and getting knocked back.
rf.menu.tip.43=Necromium tools restore health when mining blocks & slow down targets.
rf.menu.tip.44=Necromium armor weakens attackers.
rf.menu.tip.45=Various enchantments you may be used to no longer exist in RF.
rf.menu.tip.46=Etching Tables allow you to make your own music discs.
rf.menu.tip.47=Animals can eat out of Feeding Troughs and breed by themselves.
rf.menu.tip.48=Banners can be applied to Beds.
rf.menu.tip.49=Flags can be placed on Sticks and then moved up and down.
rf.menu.tip.50=Don't leave trees floating!
rf.menu.tip.51=Item Vaults combine into bigger Vaults when placed next to each other.
rf.menu.tip.52=Fluid Tanks combine into bigger Tanks when placed next to each other.
rf.menu.tip.53=Item Drawers store up to 80 stacks of a single type of item.
rf.menu.tip.54=Flutes can be assigned to tamed mobs and call them from far away.
rf.menu.tip.55=Some fungi planted on Rich Soil will grow into colonies.
rf.menu.tip.56=Furnace Boats can be fueled with Coal to go faster.
rf.menu.tip.57=Furnace Minecarts will load chunks when fueled.
rf.menu.tip.58=Lighting Copper-related blocks on fire will create green Cupric fire.
rf.menu.tip.59=Hollow Logs let you crawl inside them by sneaking next to them.
rf.menu.tip.60=Ice drops Ice Cubes when mined with a Pickaxe. They're crunchy.
rf.menu.tip.61=Killing various mobs with Knives may cause them to drop extra items.
rf.menu.tip.62=Days and nights are longer in RF.
rf.menu.tip.63=Stripping Maple Logs sometimes reveals Sap that you can bottle.
rf.menu.tip.64=Stripping Jungle Logs sometimes reveals Latex that you can bottle.
rf.menu.tip.65=Stripping Rosewood Logs sometimes reveals Latex that you can bottle.
rf.menu.tip.66=Stressometers visualise the stress level of your machines.
rf.menu.tip.67=Speedometers visualise the speed of your machines.
rf.menu.tip.68=Minecart Couplings allow you to link Minecarts together.
rf.menu.tip.69=Watermelons cause you to spit seeds when consumed.
rf.menu.tip.70=Wildfires drop Infernal Scrap.
rf.menu.tip.71=Piglin Brutes drop Infernal Scrap.
rf.menu.tip.72=Piglins and Hoglins can be made immune to zombification with a Golden Apple.
rf.menu.tip.73=Zombified Piglins and Zoglins can be cured with Weakness and a Golden Apple.
rf.menu.tip.74=Pikes come in various sizes and colors.
rf.menu.tip.75=Rough gems can be polished with Sand Paper or a Grindstone.
rf.menu.tip.76=Potato Cannons use various foods as ammo.
rf.menu.tip.77=Presents allow you to gift a stack of items to a player.
rf.menu.tip.78=Trapped Presents instantly release their contents when opened.
rf.menu.tip.79=Redstone Links transmit Redstone signals wirelessly.
rf.menu.tip.80=Rerack your trees!
rf.menu.tip.81=Bundles, Sacks, Backpacks and Terrabins let you carry more items.
rf.menu.tip.82=Bundles, Sacks, Backpacks and Terrabins can all be dyed.
rf.menu.tip.83=Terrabins can be opened from inside the inventory by right-clicking on them.
rf.menu.tip.84=Schematicannons can build for you when provided with blueprints and materials.
rf.menu.tip.85=Skillets can be held or placed over fire to cook food on the go.
rf.menu.tip.86=Skillets, Cooking Pots and Ovens always drop items or containers to their right.
rf.menu.tip.87=All hail the Slabfish.
rf.menu.tip.88=Baby Snails drop Snail Shell Pieces when they grow into adults.
rf.menu.tip.89=Mountain Boots allow you to move faster over snowy blocks.
rf.menu.tip.90=Soap can clean dye off blocks.
rf.menu.tip.91=Stoves are like Campfires, except they have 6 spaces instead of 4.
rf.menu.tip.92=Too many machines attached to a single power source may cause overstress.
rf.menu.tip.93=Suspicious Stews can only be obtained from loot and Shiitake Mooshrooms.
rf.menu.tip.94=You can find Wild Tea in Swamps and Wild Coffee in Basalt Deltas.
rf.menu.tip.95=You can find Wild Eggplants in Jungles and Rainforests.
rf.menu.tip.96=Thrashers roam Deep Frozen Oceans and attack if they locate you.
rf.menu.tip.97=Torch Arrows place Torches where they land or light mobs they hit on fire.
rf.menu.tip.98=Rose Gold Arrows fly far and knock mobs away.
rf.menu.tip.99=Steel Arrows are heavy and deal more damage.
rf.menu.tip.100=Lachryte Arrows swap you and your target's places.
rf.menu.tip.101=Trains allow for mass item transport and highly stylish travel.
rf.menu.tip.102=The wood type of Water Wheels can be changed by right-clicking with Planks.
rf.menu.tip.103=There are numerous wood types in RF. Which one's your favorite?
rf.menu.tip.104=Shearing Yaks yields Yak Hair, but it'll also make them angry at you.
rf.menu.tip.105=Shearing Bears yields Bear Fur, but it'll also make them angry at you.
rf.menu.tip.106=Shearing Mooblooms yields a few Buttercups and turn them into regular Cows.
rf.menu.tip.107=Awoken Exopearls fly towards ruined structures.
rf.menu.tip.108=Spirited Exopearls fly towards structures with spawners.
rf.menu.tip.109=Hand a Binding Exopearl to another player to easily locate them.
rf.menu.tip.110=Using Scaffolding can make building easier.
rf.menu.tip.111=Lead can be used as an alternative to Iron in some recipes.
rf.menu.tip.112=Compasses, Depth Gauges, Atlases and Spyglasses are helpful to bring along.
rf.menu.tip.113=Paragliders allow for slower descension.
rf.menu.tip.114=Smoke from fires boost you up when using a Paraglider.
rf.menu.tip.115=Koi fish reduce hostile mob spawns in an area.
rf.menu.tip.116=Large Obsidian spikes in the Nether are easy sources of Blazes.
rf.menu.tip.117=Blaze Spawners fill empty Blaze Burners when right-clicked.
rf.menu.tip.118=Cages allow you to capture smaller mobs.
rf.menu.tip.119=The Nether is a lot taller and denser than normal.
rf.menu.tip.120=Bronze has musical properties.
rf.menu.tip.121=Use Display Boards to display specific information about your machinery.
rf.menu.tip.122=Steam Engines provide large amounts of stress capacity.
rf.menu.tip.123=Lava oceans in the Nether are big enough to pump out an infinite amount of lava.
rf.menu.tip.124=Trains go through Nether Portals if there's a track on the other side.
rf.menu.tip.125=Unstable Spawners spawn a horde of mobs which will drop extra goodies.
rf.menu.tip.126=Craft Lightning Rods to redirect lightning, or create a cute buddy.
rf.menu.tip.127=Large Boats carry higher amounts of passengers or larger ones.
rf.menu.tip.128=Crawling through tight spaces can be useful in sticky situations.
rf.menu.tip.129=Various recipes leave behind byproducts.
rf.menu.tip.130=Sculk Shriekers give you three warnings before releasing the beast.
rf.menu.tip.131=Ancient Cities contain high amounts of loot.
rf.menu.tip.132=Deep in underwater caves, you may find groups of Nautili swimming around.
rf.menu.tip.133=Hostile mobs become neutral on Easy difficulty.
rf.menu.tip.134=Mimes copy your held item - and worn armor, if they hit you.
rf.menu.tip.135=Deepers explode and destroy terrain, but are only found underground.
rf.menu.tip.136=While Creepers don't destroy blocks, Deepers do.
rf.menu.tip.137=Peepers only move when you're not looking.
rf.menu.tip.138=Cameras allow you to capture precious moments.
rf.menu.tip.139=Leather can be cut into scraps and used more efficiently.
rf.menu.tip.140=Glow Ink Sacs can heal Dead Coral.
rf.menu.tip.141=Cattails grow best on Mud.
rf.menu.tip.142=Brushes allow you to brush some animals for drops.
rf.menu.tip.143=Glue Brushes can glue blocks together.
rf.menu.tip.144=Wax Brushes can wax loads of blocks at once.
rf.menu.tip.145=Pressing Shift + T while hovering over an item will share it in chat.
rf.menu.tip.146=Feeding a Golden Carrot to a Pig will make it find Truffles.
rf.menu.tip.147=Feeding Corn Kernels to Chickens, Ducks or Turkeys will make them find Buried Bugs.
rf.menu.tip.148=Worms shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.149=Spider Legs shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.150=Grubs decently shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.151=Minnows decently shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.152=Fireflies decently shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.153=Caterpillars significantly shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.154=Golden Worms significantly shorten the time it takes to catch a fish.
rf.menu.tip.155=Tackle Boxes can customise Reinforced Fishing Rods.
rf.menu.tip.156=Different Hooks have a different impact on the fishing experience.
rf.menu.tip.157=Grappling Hooks will make Reinforced Fishing Rods act like grapnels.
rf.menu.tip.158=Holding a Bucket of Water in the off-hand will make caught fish go in it.
rf.menu.tip.159=Copper and Gold can be hammered into Sheets, with a chance of breaking.
rf.menu.tip.160=Copper Golems are created with a Carved Pumpkin and a Lightning Rod.
rf.menu.tip.161=Tuff Golems are created with a Carved Pumpkin, any Wool and a Tuff block.
rf.menu.tip.162=Crops can be harvested by right-clicking them.
rf.menu.tip.163=Ores cannot be destroyed by explosions.
rf.menu.tip.164=Some Mechanical Crafting recipes require Slot Covers for empty slots.
rf.menu.tip.165=Some Mechanical Crafting recipes require a Redstone pulse to activate.

